WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.850
To most people,
mushroom clouds mean nuclear explosions:

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:05.540
the threat of radioactive fallout,

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.130
of mutually assured destruction
and of the end of the world.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:10.720
But they don't have to be:

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.610
any large enough explosion
will cause a mushroom cloud.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.450
And it's happened in Britain: right here.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:21.980
This crater was once RAF Fauld,
an old mining operation

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.610
converted to an underground bomb storage depot
for the Royal Air Force.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.840
Underground storage was meant to be safer:

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.600
one of the problems with munitions dumps is
that the enemy

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.949
just needs to hit them with one bomb and the
whole lot goes up.

00:00:35.949 --> 00:00:39.699
This site seemed perfect:
but there was a problem.

00:00:39.699 --> 00:00:43.370
Because this was built in the 1930s
for small bombs,

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.160
the sort that one person can carry,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.809
the sort that you can move on a conveyor belt,

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:51.260
the sort that the Army can fire from
a field gun across the trenches.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:56.659
That's why these old quarries with all their
tunnels and caverns were perfect.

00:00:56.659 --> 00:00:58.750
But then the Second World War moved on,

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.710
and bombing became a job for the Air Force,

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:06.880
and the bombs got bigger and bigger and bigger,
fast: half a ton, one ton, two tons.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.280
And the war effort needed many, many
more bombs than had been predicted.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.719
Rapid changes in supply and demand meant that
the underground depots were filled

00:01:15.719 --> 00:01:18.870
far beyond anything like their original capacity.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:25.579
By the end of 1944, the men here at RAF Fauld
were storing stacks of high incendiary bombs

00:01:25.579 --> 00:01:28.939
outside the mine
until they could find space inside.

00:01:28.939 --> 00:01:30.759
There was a war on.

00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:32.770
They had to make it work.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:35.530
Monday, 27th November, 1944.

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:38.430
The commanding officer was on leave.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:41.590
The officer responsible for the underground
stores was also on leave --

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:44.259
and it was his deputy's day off too.

00:01:44.259 --> 00:01:50.219
Everyone who was down in the depot and in
charge was inexperienced and massively overworked.

00:01:50.219 --> 00:01:52.229
According to the official inquiry,

00:01:52.229 --> 00:01:58.140
someone tried to remove a detonator from a
live bomb with a brass chisel.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.789
And brass chisels cause sparks.

00:02:01.789 --> 00:02:07.439
In Morocco, 1500 miles away, seismographs
recorded what felt like a distant earthquake.

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:11.840
A hundred miles away, people heard a rumble
carried on the wind.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:15.020
Four miles away,
a shock wave blasted out windows.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:19.690
And here: a mushroom cloud rose into the sky.

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:23.681
4,000 tonnes of bombs had gone up
in one terrible chain reaction,

00:02:23.681 --> 00:02:26.670
the largest explosion ever
in the British Isles.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:30.840
This crater was once a hill,
with a farmhouse on top of it:

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.260
no trace of that farmhouse, or the people
who lived there, was ever found.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.400
The bombs that hadn't immediately exploded
were thrown into the air

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:41.030
and rained down for miles around, along with
millions of tons of debris.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:47.710
A nearby dam collapsed, sending floodwaters
down into factories and houses in a nearby valley.

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:52.760
The exact death toll will never be known;
at least 60, perhaps 90.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:57.170
It took months before all the bodies were
recovered, and some were never found.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:03.300
And in the Air Force reports, held classified
for years and years after the explosion,

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.160
along with the names of the dead
and page after page

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.150
itemising every bit of the destruction,
there is this phrase:

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:17.400
"columns of black smoke and debris rose in
gigantic mushroom form".

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.250
When you're rushed, when you're inexperienced,
anyone can get complacent,

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:25.200
anyone can cut corners,
anyone can make a mistake.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.980
Even working with high explosives.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:33.290
Now slowly, over years, the crater was cleared
and reclaimed; decades later,

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:36.640
what remains is an odd scar on the landscape.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:40.730
About half the bomb store actually managed
to survive the explosion;

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:47.960
and while the bombs were removed, there are still
tunnels and storage rooms hidden under the crater.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:52.320
But after careless explorers
started damaging the site,

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.200
all the known entrances were filled in.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:58.220
And given the warnings about unexploded bombs
still in the crater,

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:02.870
I'm not about to climb this fence
and go any further.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.620
There is one little interesting note, though,

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:07.240
right at the end of the story:

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.400
through the late 40s and the 50s,

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:13.730
the American military kept asking for records
and details of the explosion.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.379
How big was it, exactly?

00:04:15.379 --> 00:04:20.000
What was the damage to the nearby land,
and was it by earthquake or by blast wave?

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.220
What happens if you, essentially,

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:26.860
detonate something with the yield of a tactical
nuclear bomb underground?

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:28.980
Britain never answered.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:32.320
And America went on 
to make its own mushroom clouds.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:35.620
